((tasks . (
     ("BILINGUAL-DOCUMENTATION-AUDIT" .
    ((priority . 9.0)
     (capabilities . (documentation translation audit policy))
     (origin . ecosystem)
     (context . "2026-09-08 ecosystem-wide language-debt audit (ecosystem/memory/LANGUAGE-DEBT-REGISTRY-2026-09-08.md): README.md opens with '## English' (line 39) before '## Українська' (line 55) -- English-first structural order violates language-policy.wsm's human-facing-order (ukrainian english german). Ukrainian content itself is present and complete, this is an ordering fix, not a translation gap.")
     (description . "Enforce the DOCUMENTATION LANGUAGE / МОВА ДОКУМЕНТАЦІЇ policy. Every human-authored markdown file (README, memory, plans, architecture, research) MUST have a substantive Ukrainian translation. Identify English-only documents and translate them. Do not translate machine identifiers or immutable historical records. Ensure every new or edited markdown document is bilingual.")))

("MYIDEA-SWARM-CONTRACT-01" . (
    (priority . 9.9)
    (description . "DONE 2026-08-18. Added repo.my ((id my-idea) (role observer-ide), exports ecosystem-status/evidence-matrix/knowledge-graph/swarm-status, imports language-contract/isa-contract/compatibility/evidence/repo-declarations, capabilities rust/clojurescript/tauri/gui/wasm, authorities ide-ux/workspace-security/evidence-visualization, non-authorities language-semantics/isa-design/compiler-internals/shiva-canon/paninian-ontology/hardware-implementation — same format as fpga-lisp/shiva-sutras/my-lisp-panini). Added ecosystem/README.md scaffold explaining why no ecosystem/imports/*.my files are populated (my-idea reads contracts/evidence live off disk via src-tauri/src/ecosystem/*.rs, not as cached claims). my-idea now shows as a declared node in its own Knowledge Graph tab instead of 'no repo.my'.")
    (done . t)
  ))
  ("MYIDEA-SWARM-DASHBOARD" . (
    (priority . 9.5)
    (description . "DONE 2026-08-19. New src-tauri/src/swarm_dashboard.rs parses swarm-node's (list-members) and (list-task-state) responses (same flat-field s-expr shape as repo.my) into a structured SwarmDashboard: per-member node id/presence/roles/capabilities, cross-referenced with currently-held open tasks from the task registry, plus overall open/completed counts. New swarm_dashboard Tauri command (separate from the existing raw-string swarm_status), new SWARM tab button and eco-view/swarm-dashboard-html renderer. Response shapes captured live from the running my-idea-1 swarm-node (13 members, 271+ task registry) via raw TCP before writing the parser; 3 cargo test unit tests assert against those real captured strings (not hand-idealized fixtures) — all pass. Not yet exercised through the actual Tauri command end-to-end (would need the shadow-cljs dev server + tauri dev, not run this session), only the parsing logic and the ClojureScript compile.")
    (done . t)
  ))
  ("SWARM-STATUS-DASHBOARD-FOLLOWUP" . (
    (priority . 1.0)
    (description . "Swarm-wide duplicate of MYIDEA-SWARM-DASHBOARD (done here 2026-08-19, commit c73038c — see that task's entry above for the real implementation). The swarm journal's own SWARM-STATUS-DASHBOARD task (defined via (define-task), not from this file) is still (holder my-idea-1) (completed nil) as of 2026-08-25 — confirmed live via (task-state (task SWARM-STATUS-DASHBOARD)). Next agent connecting as my-idea-1: please (complete-task (task SWARM-STATUS-DASHBOARD) (generation 1)) to close this near-duplicate (or check the current generation first with (task-state ...) if it has moved since).")
    (done . nil)
  ))
  ("MYIDEA-KNOWLEDGE-GRAPH" . (
    (priority . 9.0)
    (description . "Phase 1 DONE 2026-08-18 (see docs/knowledge-graph-design.md, commit b13443a): repo.my-derived node/edge graph tab, src-tauri/src/ecosystem/repo_graph.rs, knowledge_graph Tauri command, eco-view/knowledge-graph-html. Phase 2 (individual epistemic claims with PROVED/FALSIFIED/UNRESOLVED status, drift highlighting between shiva-sutras' claims-export.yaml and my-lisp-panini's ecosystem/imports/*.my) intentionally deferred, tracked in the design doc, not restated as a separate tasks.my entry.")
    (done . t)
  ))
  ("IDEA-PROTOCOL-DRIFT-FIX" . (
    (priority . 9.8)
    (description . "DONE 2026-08-18. Rewrote AGENTS.md's Coordination channels section to state plainly that swarm-node is the coordination layer (P2P mesh, no relaying) and :9999 is oracle-only (eval/parse/diagnose/contract-version) — matching fpga-lisp/AGENTS.md's wording. Added my-idea-1's own join/sync-tasks commands (port 9104) and a note that src-tauri/src/swarm.rs already talks to swarm-node directly, reading one line without waiting for EOF (unlike oracle.rs's one-shot :9999 client).")
    (done . t)
  ))
  ("IDEA-CONTRACT-VERSION-DRIFT-CHECK" . (
    (priority . 8.5)
    (description . "DONE 2026-08-18, no drift found. Grepped AGENTS.md/docs/README for hardcoded language-contract version claims: my-idea's own docs (system-observatory-status.md, system-observatory-vision.md) only reference language-contract.my/isa-contract.my/compatibility.my by filename, never hardcode a version number — contracts.rs reads them live at runtime via the my_lisp crate's own reader, not a saved-off number. The submodule's actual contract (external/my-lisp/language-contract.my) is currently (major . 2) (minor . 0). No fix needed; this repo was already doing it right.")
    (done . t)
  ))
  ("IDEA-SUBAGENT-DOCTRINE" . (
    (priority . 6.0)
    (description . "DONE 2026-08-18. Added 'Subagents and specialist models' section to AGENTS.md: independent subagents for audits/verification not parallel coding, never bias a verifier with the preferred answer, external specialist models (Sarvam etc.) are hypothesis sources not authoritative evidence, points to shiva-sutras/docs/sarvam-integration-guide.md for Sarvam operating details rather than duplicating them here.")
    (done . t)
  ))
  ("IDEA-APPIMAGE-XDG-UTILS" . (
    (priority . 4.0)
    (description . "PARTIAL 2026-08-18. Installed xdg-utils natively (sudo apt-get install -y xdg-utils) — /usr/bin/xdg-open now exists, confirmed via `which xdg-open`. Tried adding \"xdg-utils\" to manifest.scm's Guix package list first: broke pkg-config resolution for gio-sys (profile rebuild left pkg-config unfindable) — reverted, documented as a known-bad approach in manifest.scm's comments, native apt install is the working path (matches how Bun/build-essential/rustup are handled). NOT closing: re-running bun run tauri build afterward hit a *different*, pre-existing pkg-config failure (gio-sys/gobject-sys can't find pkg-config even with the reverted manifest) that also blocked the deb/rpm steps this time, unrelated to xdg-utils — see new IDEA-PKG-CONFIG-REGRESSION. Re-verify AppImage specifically once that's fixed.")
    (done . ())
  ))
  ("IDEA-PKG-CONFIG-REGRESSION" . (
    (priority . 9.5)
    (description . "ROOT-CAUSED 2026-08-18. bun run tauri build (and plain cargo check) intermittently fail with 'The pkg-config command could not be found' inside gio-sys/gobject-sys build scripts, specifically when entering the environment via `guix time-machine -C ../my-lisp/channels.scm -- shell -m manifest.scm` — repro'd 3x. Switching to plain `guix shell -m manifest.scm` (same manifest.scm, no time-machine channel pin) made cargo check pass clean on the first try, compiling the new ecosystem/repo_graph.rs module with zero errors. Root cause: guix time-machine re-fetches/re-authenticates the pinned channel (visible 'channel guix lacks an introduction' warning) and appears to rebuild a working profile whose pkg-config isn't correctly wired into cargo build-script subprocess PATH — a time-machine-specific profile-construction bug, not a missing package (pkg-config IS present and `which pkg-config` resolves fine in both cases). Workaround: prefer plain `guix shell -m manifest.scm` for iterative cargo check/build; reserve time-machine for when the rustc-too-old blocker actually requires the pinned rust 1.93.0 (see AGENTS.md's rustc-too-old section) — document this distinction in AGENTS.md.")
    (done . t)
  ))
  ("IDEA-PLAYWRIGHT-BROWSER-SETUP" . (
    (priority . 4.0)
    (description . "bun run test fails 1 of 37 subtests on a fresh environment ('Standalone web artifact does not stack overflow on 100k list', tests/smoke.test.mjs:205) with 'browserType.launch: Executable doesn't exist ... chrome-headless-shell'. Needs 'bunx playwright install' as a documented one-time setup step (AGENTS.md and/or CI) so clean-install verification doesn't need manual intervention to fully pass. DONE: commit a865ed5 (2026-08-22) documents the step in AGENTS.md:277-280, verified end-to-end (build EXIT=0, npm test 37/37 PASS); CI (.github/workflows/ci.yml:40) already runs 'bunx playwright install chromium --with-deps'.")
    (done . t)
  ))
  ("IDEA-PUSH-BUN-MIGRATION" . (
