    (priority . 5.0)
    (description . "Per docs/manus-ai-review-analysis.md (2026-08-18, analyzing external Manus AI reviews): tests/eco-panel.test.mjs only exercises the Playwright UI against mocked data, so it proves layout, not correctness of ecosystem_status/knowledge_graph's actual data derivation from disk. Add a real native Tauri integration test: build a temporary sibling-repo directory layout (fake my-lisp/fpga-lisp/cml/shiva-sutras/my-lisp-panini with known repo.my/contract files), call ecosystem::status()/ecosystem::knowledge_graph() directly, assert on the structured output. Cheap, concrete, catches real regressions in the repo_graph.rs/contracts.rs/evidence.rs parsers that mocked frontend tests cannot.")
    (done . ())
  ))
  ("IDEA-SARVAM-VERIFY-I18N-STRINGS" . (
    (priority . 7.0)
    (description . "DONE (first pass) 2026-08-19. See docs/sarvam-i18n-verification.md: checked 4 of ~20+ i18n.cljs strings (uk+de :ast label, uk+de amber theme name) via cold single-fact Sarvam calls, no max_tokens. Finding: both uk 'Лабораторія мов / AST' and de 'Sprachlabor / AST' independently got the same stylistic note (grammatically correct, but a literal-metaphor translation of 'Language Lab') — kept as-is, a deliberate name choice matching the product's own 'Language Lab' terminology, not a translation error; documented as a recorded disagreement per the task's own instruction, not silently accepted or silently changed. Theme names (Бурштин/Bernstein for Amber) confirmed idiomatic, no issue. Remaining ~16 strings (other UI labels, other theme names) not yet sampled — future pass if desired, not blocking.")
    (done . t)
  ))
